    "body": "Not sure about Chrome, but at the moment in Firefox I think all our channel / request ids are either based on counters or timestamps - no uuid. Internally, to avoid clashes, in Firefox's BiDi implementation we prefix them with a uuid representing the process which owns the request, but that's it.\r\n\r\nStill, I'm happy to specify this as UUID, I think it's a reasonable model, and the implementations should be able to get there.",
